---
/* L53 - two providers that agree, and the gap below. One writer: the figures workstream C. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L53.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a conveyor belt carrying two rectangular cards under two stamp presses, each press marking a circled cross onto its card, with a third loose card on the floor marked with a circled triangle."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L53-fig-title L53-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L53-fig-title">Two models on the same side of the line, far apart underneath</title>
      <desc id="L53-fig-desc">
        A horizontal probability scale with a dashed marker at 0.5. Two filled dots sit above the line, one at 0.52 and one at 0.88, and a bracket drawn above them spans the distance between them, labelled gap 0.36. Below the scale, a solid rule labelled labels records that both models are above 0.5 and therefore agree, and a dashed rule labelled but records that the confidence underneath is far apart. The dots pulse after the bracket has drawn itself.
      </desc>
      <line x1="120" y1="150" x2="560" y2="150" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="340" y1="96" x2="340" y2="196" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
      <text x="330" y="88" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.5</text>

      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 186; --m-duration: 1s;" d="M 349 118 L 349 106 L 507 106 L 507 118" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="404" y="98" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">gap 0.36</text>

      <circle class="m-pulse" style="--m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 0.5s;" cx="349" cy="150" r="6" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      <circle class="m-pulse" style="--m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 0.5s;" cx="507" cy="150" r="6" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      <text x="324" y="176" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">A 0.52</text>
      <text x="482" y="176" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">B 0.88</text>

      <line x1="120" y1="230" x2="560" y2="230" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="40" y="234" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">labels:</text>
      <text x="120" y="248" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">both above 0.5, so they agree</text>

      <line x1="120" y1="272" x2="560" y2="272" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
      <text x="40" y="276" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">but:</text>
      <text x="120" y="290" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">the confidence underneath is far apart</text>

      <text x="40" y="322" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">agreement is a label; the gap underneath it is the measurement</text>

    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L53</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">Two providers can agree on the label and still sit 0.36 apart in confidence, so agreement and the size of the gap are two different measurements.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
